# The Docker build context is `.` and the only inputs the image needs are `Cargo.toml`,
# `Cargo.lock` and `src/`. Everything else is either rebuilt, irrelevant to a release
# build, or large — `target/` alone is tens of gigabytes.
#
# Unlike `.gitignore`, a pattern without a slash matches one level only, so the
# directory patterns below are anchored with a leading slash on purpose.
/target
/.git
/.tact

/docs
/examples
/plugins
/scripts
/tests
/tools

# A local `.env` must never reach an image (nothing here reads one, but the next
# `COPY . .` would not be so lucky).
.env
.env.*
